== frame
+   holst object add frame <board> [<text>] [flags]
+   -w, --workspace ws       Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
+       --frame frame        Put it inside this frame: id, link, title or part of a title; --at counts from its corner
+       --at x,y             The top-left corner in board units, from the frame's corner with --frame; a free corner by default
+       --size w,h           The size as width,height, e.g. 260,160; the kind's own size by default; an image's own size, at most 1000 on the long side, by default; an icon's is square, 48,48 by default
+   -c, --color color        The fill, or an arrow's line color: a palette token, e.g. yellow4; a task's: gray, green, yellow, orange, red, violet, blue, sky, lime or pink; a drawing's line: a palette token; #1E1E1E (#FBF040 highlighter) by default; the kind's own color by default; an icon takes gray12, gray8, red9, orange9, yellow9, lime9, green9, mint9, blue9, indigo9, violet9 or pink9
+       --ratio ratio        A frame's ratio: 16:9, 4:3, 1:1, a4 or a4-landscape; with --size the area is kept; 16:9 at 1920x1080 and the like by default
+       --background style   A frame's background: fill, border or outline; border by default
+       --hide-content       Hide the content of a frame; needs the board's right to hide frame content
+       --items file         Many in one write: a JSON array or JSON lines file, - for stdin; its keys are the flags of one call
+   -n, --dry-run            Show what would change; change nothing
+   $ holst o add frame "Roadmap" "Q4" --items q4.json
-   holst object add sticker <board> [<text>] [flags]
-       --text-format format   How the text is read: plain, or markdown for headings, lists, checkboxes, links and bold, italic, strike marks; plain by default
-   -w, --workspace ws         Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
-       --frame frame          Put it inside this frame: id, link, title or part of a title; --at counts from its corner
-       --at x,y               The top-left corner in board units, from the frame's corner with --frame; a free corner by default
-       --size w,h             The size as width,height, e.g. 260,160; the kind's own size by default; an image's own size, at most 1000 on the long side, by default; an icon's is square, 48,48 by default
-   -c, --color color          The fill, or an arrow's line color: a palette token, e.g. yellow4; a task's: gray, green, yellow, orange, red, violet, blue, sky, lime or pink; a drawing's line: a palette token; #1E1E1E (#FBF040 highlighter) by default; the kind's own color by default; an icon takes gray12, gray8, red9, orange9, yellow9, lime9, green9, mint9, blue9, indigo9, violet9 or pink9
-       --items file           Many in one write: a JSON array or JSON lines file, - for stdin; its keys are the flags of one call
-   -n, --dry-run              Show what would change; change nothing
-   $ holst o add sticker "Roadmap" "Ask design" -c yellow4
== arrow
+   holst object add arrow <board> [flags]
+       --from object          The object an arrow starts at: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id; with --items also #N, an earlier item
+       --to object            The object an arrow points to: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id; with --items also #N, an earlier item
+       --line line            An arrow's line: straight, elbow or curved; elbow by default
+       --heads start,end      An arrow's heads, e.g. none,triangle-filled: none, figma, miro, arc, triangle-filled, triangle, circle-filled, circle, rhombus-filled, rhombus, stick, stick-stick, triadius, triadius-stick, triadius-circle, stick-circle or slash; an empty side keeps that end; none,miro by default
+       --stroke-style style   An arrow's line: solid, dashed or dotted; solid by default
+       --stroke-width n       An arrow's line width: 1, 1.5, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 13 or 17; 2 by default; a drawing's: a whole 1 to 30, 3 (highlighter 22) by default
+       --label text[@pos]     An arrow's label, repeat for several; text@0.25 puts it a quarter of the way from the start, in the middle by default
+   $ holst o add arrow "Roadmap" --from a1b2c3d4 --to e5f6a7b8
-   holst object add sticker <board> [<text>] [flags]
-   text    The text; lines become paragraphs; the title of a frame or task; the code of a code block; the name of an icon, e.g. rocket-launch
-       --text-format format   How the text is read: plain, or markdown for headings, lists, checkboxes, links and bold, italic, strike marks; plain by default
-       --at x,y               The top-left corner in board units, from the frame's corner with --frame; a free corner by default
-       --size w,h             The size as width,height, e.g. 260,160; the kind's own size by default; an image's own size, at most 1000 on the long side, by default; an icon's is square, 48,48 by default
-   $ holst o add sticker "Roadmap" "Ask design" -c yellow4
== link
+   holst object add link <board> [<url>] [flags]
+   url     The page to link to, e.g. https://example.com
+   -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
+       --frame frame    Put it inside this frame: id, link, title or part of a title; --at counts from its corner
+       --at x,y         The top-left corner in board units, from the frame's corner with --frame; a free corner by default
+       --no-preview     Keep the card plain even when the page can be embedded
+       --items file     Many in one write: a JSON array or JSON lines file, - for stdin; its keys are the flags of one call
+   -n, --dry-run        Show what would change; change nothing
+   $ holst o add link "Roadmap" https://example.com
