== reaction-stamp
+   holst object add reaction-stamp <board> [flags]
+   -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
+       --frame frame    Put it inside this frame: id, link, title or part of a title; --at counts from its corner
+       --at x,y         The top-left corner in board units, from the frame's corner with --frame; a free corner by default
+       --on object      The object a reaction stamp sticks to and goes onto: a shape, sticker, document, task or image; id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id; --at counts from its corner, else the stamp goes to its middle; a loose stamp without it
+       --reaction key   A reaction stamp's picture: like, heart, star, +1, dislike, figma-question, check or cross; like by default
+       --items file     Many in one write: a JSON array or JSON lines file, - for stdin; its keys are the flags of one call
+   -n, --dry-run        Show what would change; change nothing
